WEBVTT

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.880
Is Mt. Omuro far from here?

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:10.990
It's about an hour's drive.

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.320
We're stopping by Iida-san's shop first, right?

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.560
Yup.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.990
Let's hang out at Mt. Omuro until noon or so,
then head to the cactus park.

00:00:20.210 --> 00:00:22.870
Then we can see the capybaras 
Akari-chan's been waiting for!

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.180
I can't wait to see them, either!

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:27.610
Let's hurry back to the van!

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.630
She's so full of energy.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:33.620
Thanks.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.830
For inviting me.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.140
I had fun.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:42.460
What brought this on?

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:45.040
We still have lots to do, Rin-chan.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.090
That's right.

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:48.110
The day's just getting started.

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:33.000
<b>(2) Episode 13
 I'm Home</b>

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:30.920
There's Mt. Omuro.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:35.660
That dark, black one?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.930
It's normally a green mountain 
covered in silvergrass,

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:41.610
but there was apparently a 
controlled burn just last month.

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:42.510
Huh...

00:02:43.100 --> 00:02:47.220
Good thing the campground offered 
to look after your bike, huh?

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:48.040
Yeah.

00:02:48.660 --> 00:02:49.520
But...

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:54.260
Seven people plus luggage is pretty tight.

00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:58.780
Hello!

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:00.160
Welcome.

00:03:00.160 --> 00:03:02.410
Thanks for coming all the 
way out from Yamanashi.

00:03:02.410 --> 00:03:03.280
Welcome.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.840
Thank you so much for your 
help at Lake Yamanaka.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:08.870
Not at all.

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.170
It was fun having such a big crowd.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:13.990
Looks like there's even more of you today.

00:03:13.990 --> 00:03:16.500
These are our friends from school.

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:18.670
Oh, yeah? That's nice.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:23.220
I used to travel with my friends 
a lot when I was younger, too.

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.430
Really?

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:29.770
This is wine and some raisin 
sandwiches from Yamanashi.

00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:31.940
Thank you.

00:03:32.390 --> 00:03:36.360
The campsite you introduced us to 
turned out to be really nice, too.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.690
Of course.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:41.630
That area's famous for having 
the prettiest sunset in Japan.

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:43.570
It was gorgeous!

00:03:43.950 --> 00:03:45.410
Have you tried the alfonsino yet?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:47.970
Yeah! We had alfonsino burgers.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:50.840
We also made acqua pazza
 with dried alfonsino.

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:52.680
Rin-chan, look over there!

00:03:55.150 --> 00:03:56.200
That's...

00:03:58.220 --> 00:04:00.710
Choko-chan!

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.720
Long time no see, Choko!

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:09.320
Choko-chan...

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.100
<i>I'm getting déjà vu.</i>

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.100
There, there, Chikuwa!

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.920
Oh, sorry. You're Choko-chan.

00:04:17.500 --> 00:04:20.610
Ena-chan's starting to go through
 Chikuwa withdrawal.

00:04:21.130 --> 00:04:23.110
So, what's the plan from here?

00:04:23.650 --> 00:04:25.180
Are you headed back to Yamanashi?

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:28.290
No, we're going up to Mt. Omuro and...

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.520
Yes! We're going to see the 
capybaras in the hot spring!

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.250
Oh? That so?

00:04:33.620 --> 00:04:36.400
Maybe I should go with you to Mt. Omuro.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:38.050
I'd like to walk Choko.

00:04:38.050 --> 00:04:39.880
Great! Let's go!

00:04:46.680 --> 00:05:03.150
Mt. Omuro

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:51.040
<i>Geospot number twelve: Mt. Omuro.</i>

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:57.830
<i>A silvergrass-covered volcano 
in Itou peaking at 500 meters.</i>

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.150
<i>A controlled burn takes place every February.</i>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:08.410
<b>I
c
e

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.410
<b>Brain Freeze</b>

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.680
What a nice view.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:23.630
Indeed.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:26.920
It really is all black.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.930
It's freshly burnt.

00:05:29.410 --> 00:05:33.160
I heard they have different mascots 
for the different seasons here.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:34.810
Mascots?

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:37.560
<b>Spring & Summer</b>

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.190
Matcha pudding.

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.690
<b>Fall</b>

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.590
Hojicha pudding.

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.480
<b>Winter</b>

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.720
Coffee jelly.

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.150
<b>Spring & Summer</b>

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.150
<b>Winter</b>

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.150
<b>Fall</b>

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:44.150
You're right!

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:46.040
<i>Say cheese!</i>

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:48.700
<b>Keepsake Photos</b>

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:54.800
You both look so shocked!

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.210
They really do.

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.070
That thing was taking souvenir photos?

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:02.000
That startled me.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:06.220
I think I'll buy one, though. It's funny.

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:07.470
Me too, then.

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:12.810
This feels so liberating!

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:14.780
The view's great!

00:06:14.780 --> 00:06:17.480
Looks like that's the peak over there.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:22.500
All right, Nadeshiko, Mini Inuko!
First one to the peak wins!

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.230
Bring it on!

00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:25.480
Yeah! Yeah!

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:27.700
Ready...

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:28.990
Go!

00:06:30.490 --> 00:06:31.870
Just kidding!

00:06:33.190 --> 00:06:34.240
Guys! Wait!

00:06:34.420 --> 00:06:36.350
Don't leave me!

00:06:36.350 --> 00:06:38.750
No running! It's dangerous!

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:44.660
It's pretty chilly for the 
relatively low altitude.

00:06:46.170 --> 00:06:51.260
It's nice and cool in the summer,
so I often bring Choko up here for walks.

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:52.510
I see.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.720
He perks right up whenever we come.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:07:00.270
Ah, right. Corgis don't like hot weather.

00:07:03.370 --> 00:07:05.270
<i>Such a cute butt!</i>

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.070
Yatsugatake Jizo Statues

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:14.020
Made it.

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:23.360
What a great view.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:26.440
I know.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.260
What's this?

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:43.170
It says it's a triangulation point.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:45.290
To serve as a reference 
point for measurements.

00:07:45.290 --> 00:07:47.290
Huh...

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.320
What is that, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:56.580
I... made it...

00:07:58.620 --> 00:07:59.390
Stop it!

00:07:59.390 --> 00:08:00.830
Don't make me laugh!

00:08:00.830 --> 00:08:03.580
I'm dying!

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.600
Here we go, everyone.

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:08.110
Okay!

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:17.460
Nice to know you can see 
Mt. Fuji from Mt. Omuro, too.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:18.970
You sure can.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:24.680
In fact, the gods worshipped at 
Mt. Fuji and Mt. Omuro are sisters.

00:08:24.680 --> 00:08:26.230
Really?

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:28.480
But they don't get along very well at all.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:33.080
Apparently, you'll be cursed if you 
praise Mt. Fuji from atop Mt. Omuro.

00:08:36.960 --> 00:08:38.950
It's just an urban legend.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.690
<b>Itou Cactus Park</b>

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.690
<b>Welcome</b>

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:44.690
<b>Vehicle Entrance</b>

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.680
Finally...

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:50.160
We finally get to meet the capybaras!

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:53.380
Akari-chan's been looking 
forward to this the whole time.

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:55.680
Look, peacocks!

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.100
And pelicans over there.

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.270
What kind of monkey is that?

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.570
Wow.

00:09:02.570 --> 00:09:05.720
They're roaming free right at the gate.

00:09:05.720 --> 00:09:08.170
Pelicans are so elegant.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:12.570
Please buy your admission tickets 
at the vending machine over there.

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:19.130
I love that the animals here roam free 
right up to the edge of the property.

00:09:19.130 --> 00:09:19.870
What?

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:22.700
Iguchi-kun, they're on the loose again!

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.530
Roger! I'm on it!

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.930
<i>So they aren't free range?</i>

00:09:51.530 --> 00:09:55.170
Akari-chan, the capybara 
hot spring is just up ahead.

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:56.320
Really?

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:57.260
Aki-chan!

00:09:57.260 --> 00:09:58.320
All right, let's go!

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.630
You're gonna fall if you run, you two.

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:04.650
You tripped again?

00:10:04.650 --> 00:10:05.500
Yeah.

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:18.840
<b>Outdoor Capybara Bath</b>

00:10:23.160 --> 00:10:27.100
They look so pleased in the hot spring.

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:30.270
This is so healing.

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:32.110
It really is.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:36.320
The way you can't tell if they're
awake or asleep is just...

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:38.530
It's indescribable.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.610
It's making <i>me</i> feel relaxed, too.

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:43.890
Haaahh...

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:45.370
Huh?!

00:10:47.960 --> 00:10:53.380
Akari-chan, there's an area over there 
where you can pet the capybaras.

00:10:53.510 --> 00:10:54.920
I'll go!

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:59.380
I have a feeling you'd follow anyone 
if they baited you with capybaras.

00:11:12.210 --> 00:11:16.060
Akari-chan! They sell capybara plushies!

00:11:13.150 --> 00:11:17.110
<b>Capybara Corner</b>

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:19.220
Akari-chan, it's a capybara hoodie!

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:22.590
Akari-chan, they have capybara snacks, too.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.030
<b>Capybara Dumplings</b>

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.030
<b>Capybara Dumplings</b>

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.030
<b>Yuzu Flavor</b>

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.030
<b>Brown Sugar Flavor</b>

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:30.040
Aki-chan!

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:32.660
I just remembered! You haven't given 
me my New Year's allowance yet!

00:11:32.660 --> 00:11:34.290
That was such a long time ago...

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:39.840
Take care, everyone.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:42.680
You're welcome to drop by
 whenever you'd like.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:43.860
Okay.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.930
I hope you come to camp in 
Yamanashi sometime, too, Iida-san.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:50.760
You can mail order Ikeike, Sensei.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:53.200
Put in an order when you run out, okay?

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:54.450
You bet I will.

00:12:01.210 --> 00:12:05.570
Sensei, can we visit a 
gift shop on our way home?

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:06.950
Sure.

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.330
Why don't we stop at a roadside station?

00:12:09.680 --> 00:12:12.300
How many geospots did we hit?

00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.480
Let's see...

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.880
Twelve in total.

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.590
We went to quite a few.

00:12:17.850 --> 00:12:19.910
Let's do them all next time.

00:12:19.910 --> 00:12:21.880
How many are there in all?

00:12:21.880 --> 00:12:25.480
I never counted, but I think 
there were more than a hundred.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:27.220
What, seriously?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:30.970
Our Izu camp trip's almost over, huh?

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:36.080
It's been a while since we 
all went camping together.

00:12:36.080 --> 00:12:37.550
I had fun.

00:12:38.680 --> 00:12:39.860
Yeah.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.170
Now, wait.

00:12:41.170 --> 00:12:44.240
It isn't over until we're all back home.

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:45.450
She's right.

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:47.710
Don't let your guard down, Private Ena.

00:12:47.710 --> 00:12:49.040
Understood, ma'am!

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:06.840
There.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.820
Shima-san, are you sure Shuzenji 
is where you want to part ways?

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:11.850
Yes.

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:15.390
It doesn't look like I'll be able to 
drive my bike on the roads there,

00:13:15.390 --> 00:13:17.540
so I'll take my time getting back home.

00:13:17.540 --> 00:13:18.610
All right.

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:21.320
Please be careful on the road.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.940
Take a break if you get tired.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:24.790
Okay.

00:13:24.790 --> 00:13:26.110
You take care, too, Sensei.

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:28.920
Aren't you going to be lonely, Rin-chan?

00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:29.990
I'll be okay.

00:13:30.290 --> 00:13:32.990
Want to borrow my capybara plushie?

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:36.870
I'll pass on that.

00:13:37.260 --> 00:13:41.220
Rin, I'll switch places with you
 if you ever get tired.

00:13:41.780 --> 00:13:43.880
You don't even have a license.

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:49.390
Shuzenji Hot Springs

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:57.140
Okay, I'm headed this way.

00:13:57.670 --> 00:13:58.630
Rin-chan.

00:14:04.700 --> 00:14:06.370
Drive safely.

00:14:06.370 --> 00:14:07.780
I know.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.720
Let me know when you get home!

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:40.560
Kagamihara-san, you can 
nap until we get home.

00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:41.880
Nah.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:43.820
You've been driving this whole time.

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.890
I'll stay awake, too!

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:48.110
All right.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.230
There's the Izu peninsula.

00:14:54.530 --> 00:14:56.370
It's already so far away.

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:08.550
We're already home.

00:15:11.660 --> 00:15:14.420
Is that all your stuff, Nadeshiko-chan?

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:16.100
Yeah, thanks.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:19.830
I'll upload all our photos later, Nadeshiko.

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:21.350
Okay!

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:24.760
Thank you for the past three days, Sensei.

00:15:24.760 --> 00:15:26.730
I'm glad we made it home safe and sound.

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:31.050
Give Chikuwa lots of love 
when you get home, Ena-chan.

00:15:31.050 --> 00:15:32.610
You know I will!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:35.490
See you later, Nadeshiko-chan!

00:15:35.750 --> 00:15:38.040
Yeah! See you!

00:15:51.650 --> 00:15:55.080
<i>I got caught right in rush hour traffic...</i>

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:05.470
<i>I've ridden 400 kilometers since I left home?</i>

00:16:06.420 --> 00:16:09.140
<i>It'll be 450 by the time I get back.</i>

00:16:09.140 --> 00:16:10.950
<i>That's a new record.</i>

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:14.260
<i>Grandpa was right.</i>

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:16.260
<i>Izu's huge.</i>

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:35.470
<b>Inuko & Nadeshiko</b>

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:51.980
<i>I don't know if it's 
because I'm driving alone</i>

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:55.620
<i>or if the night scenery is 
making me feel this way...</i>

00:16:57.080 --> 00:16:58.740
<i>But I'm a bit lonely.</i>

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:04.580
<i>Still, the healthy exhaustion and
 the relief of being homeward bound...</i>

00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:09.090
<i>I love this feeling.</i>

00:17:17.540 --> 00:17:19.110
<i>I'm back.</i>

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:30.730
Pirate Fry

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:30.730
Squid Ink Noodles

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:30.730
<b>Two servings 
with sauce</b>

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:30.730
<b>Wasabi Mayo</b>

00:17:25.230 --> 00:17:30.730
<b>Grandchildren
 of the Waves</b>

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.560
Look at all the stuff you got!

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.470
Just how much money did you give her?

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:30.730
<b>Boar 
Buns</b>

00:17:30.920 --> 00:17:34.430
I'll make dinner with 
this dried fish tomorrow.

00:17:34.430 --> 00:17:36.150
Okay. I'm looking forward to it.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.910
I'm home!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.820
We made it back, too.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:43.120
Welcome home.

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:44.370
Welcome home!

00:17:44.760 --> 00:17:47.140
Chikuwa greeted me at the door.

00:17:47.140 --> 00:17:48.970
He looks so happy.

00:17:48.970 --> 00:17:50.130
How's Akari-chan?

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:53.290
She's eating the capybara 
dumplings we bought.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.010
She's eating those already?

00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:00.930
I'm home.

00:18:00.930 --> 00:18:02.180
Welcome back.

00:18:03.780 --> 00:18:05.800
Nadeshiko, you're home.

00:18:05.800 --> 00:18:07.640
Yeah, I'm back.

00:18:09.780 --> 00:18:11.300
What's the matter with you?

00:18:11.770 --> 00:18:14.790
Rin-chan isn't replying at all.

00:18:14.790 --> 00:18:17.150
I hope she's okay.

00:18:17.460 --> 00:18:19.350
She must be driving.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.530
You think so?

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:24.790
Is Rin not home yet?

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.790
I don't think so

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:32.170
That means the Izu camp trip isn't over yet!

00:18:30.790 --> 00:18:34.550
Yeah

00:18:32.290 --> 00:18:34.550
It isn't over until we're all home

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:39.620
Onee-chan!

00:18:46.600 --> 00:18:48.790
<i>It's still cold around here.</i>

00:18:49.850 --> 00:18:51.070
<i>Made it to Minobu.</i>

00:18:51.660 --> 00:18:53.070
<i>I'm almost there.</i>

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:55.140
Hey!

00:18:55.880 --> 00:18:57.060
Hey!

00:18:57.060 --> 00:18:58.600
Rin-chan!

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:03.780
What's wrong?

00:19:05.300 --> 00:19:07.080
I got worried because you weren't replying.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.670
I had my sister give me a ride here.

00:19:10.670 --> 00:19:11.710
Reply?

00:19:11.710 --> 00:19:12.080
Nadeshiko

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.710
We're in Yamanashi

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.710
Made it home in one piece!

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.710
Let me know when you get home

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.710
It's getting dark, so be careful

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.710
Where are you? In Yamanashi?

00:19:12.080 --> 00:19:15.710
You haven't gotten lost, have you?

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:14.040
Oh, look at that.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:15.710
So many messages.

00:19:16.150 --> 00:19:19.820
I wasn't using my phone on my 
way home, so I didn't notice.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.220
You didn't need to worry so much, though...

00:19:29.400 --> 00:19:30.390
Is something wrong?

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:31.960
Uh, no.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:35.110
<i>I guess it goes both ways.</i>

00:19:41.620 --> 00:19:44.830
Hey, what was your favorite place?

00:19:45.890 --> 00:19:47.120
Let me think...

00:19:47.710 --> 00:19:49.820
Cape Kogane was nice.

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.900
So was Hosono Plateau.

00:19:51.900 --> 00:19:54.090
Mt. Omuro was good, too.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:56.750
Mt. Omuro really was nice.

00:19:57.340 --> 00:19:59.290
So were the hot springs.

00:19:59.970 --> 00:20:02.870
And the birthday party made me so happy.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:11.770
It's kind of sad that the trip's over, huh?

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:14.920
Yeah.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:19.340
But I don't mind that so much.

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:23.430
We can always go somewhere again.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:33.040
It's still kind of lonely, though.

00:20:35.360 --> 00:20:38.550
I had so much fun.

00:20:59.050 --> 00:21:01.670
So I want to do it again.

00:21:02.800 --> 00:21:04.530
Let's go camping again!

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.830
That's what I just said.

00:21:13.530 --> 00:21:14.830
You're right.

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:20.570
Mt. Fuji is so pretty at night.

00:21:21.260 --> 00:21:24.370
I think I'll go to Lake Motosu 
on my next solo camping trip.

00:21:25.070 --> 00:21:27.990
Have you never spent the night there before?

00:21:28.690 --> 00:21:31.310
That was before I started camping.

00:21:31.310 --> 00:21:32.560
Ah.

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:37.900
Speaking of, what were you like 
on your first camping trip?

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:39.290
My first trip?

00:21:40.890 --> 00:21:42.570
It was pretty rough.

00:21:43.930 --> 00:21:47.150
I think I was in my first year of middle school.

00:22:41.250 --> 00:22:44.750
Dear Grandpa,

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:47.010
Homemade
<b>Izu Miso-Pickled Meat</b>

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:47.010
Tachibana
Meat Shop

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:36.330
Always mind the campsite 
and facility rules. Don't forget to 
take care of fires and your trash!

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:36.330
It gets cold during the winter. 
Stay warm and be well-prepared!

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:36.330
Outdoor Activities Club

00:23:25.230 --> 00:23:36.330
When camping...

00:23:35.950 --> 00:23:41.260
<b>Thanks for watching!</b>
